# Two-Axis Code Review Evidence: L4 Desktop Environment and L5 Applications
File: openOODA/audits/nextgen/axis/l4_l5_evidence.oot

Provenance: Batch 5 two-axis review. Part 1 of 2 (see `l4_l5_findings.oot` for the findings).

## 1. Scope

37 repositories: 20 in `openOODA-DE` and 17 in `openOODA-apps`, all at `origin/master`.

## 2. Build, verify, test sweep

Command per repository, with the ambient compiler overridden because the exported value in the
Makefiles is broken:

```
cd <repo> && OODA_COMPILER=/Projects/openOODA-core/oodac/bin/oodac make build
cd <repo> && OODA_COMPILER=/Projects/openOODA-core/oodac/bin/oodac make verify
cd <repo> && OODA_COMPILER=/Projects/openOODA-core/oodac/bin/oodac make test
```

Result: 35 of 37 repositories pass `build`, `verify` and `test` with exit code 0. The two
exceptions are `ootaskmgr` and `ooterm`, both of which pass standalone and both of which pass
`make verify` from a fresh clone of `origin/master`. See section 5.

